# walks/fixture.env -- the only knobs the regression walk cannot discover at runtime.
# Sourced by every family script. Every other fact about the fixture (which systems exist,
# which fleets, which technologies, which screens are registered) is read back from the
# live game, so these three are the whole configuration surface.

# The dev server. Environment, not fixture: `ES2ACCESS_DEV_PORT` moves it, and a second
# game instance would need a second port. Cannot be discovered -- it is the thing we ask.
WALK_HOST="${WALK_HOST:-http://127.0.0.1:8771}"

# Settle-time multiplier, in percent. Every `pause` is scaled by it. Cannot be discovered:
# how long a star-system page takes to draw is a property of the machine, not of the game
# state we can query. Raise it (150, 200) on a slower box if a walk starts landing early;
# a walk that is too fast shows up as a self-diff, never as an error.
WALK_PACE="${WALK_PACE:-100}"

# OPTIONAL reset mode only. `walk-all.sh --reset` issues `POST /loadsave` with this body
# before walking; empty means "the newest save", which is the dev server's own default.
# The walk NEVER loads a save on its own -- it walks whatever is already in the game.
# Cannot be discovered because "which save is the fixture" is the caller's intent.
WALK_SAVE="${WALK_SAVE:-}"
